The function takes rows and returns only the PUBLIC_COLUMNS from each, so I'll document that, including that personal fields like objector contact details are excluded. [tool_use propose_change {"path":"register/export.py","summary":"Add docstring to export_comments describing its input, output, and the public-column filtering.","diff":"--- a/register/export.py\n+++ b/register/export.py\n@@ -3,6 +3,16 @@\n PUBLIC_COLUMNS = ['reference', 'address', 'comment_date', 'stance', 'comment_text']\n \n def export_comments(rows):\n+    \"\"\"Return public-facing copies of comment rows.\n+\n+    Each row is reduced to the columns listed in PUBLIC_COLUMNS\n+    (reference, address, comment_date, stance, comment_text). All other\n+    columns, including objector contact details and internal notes, are\n+    omitted from the result.\n+\n+    Args:\n+        rows: An iterable of mappings, each containing at least the PUBLIC_COLUMNS keys.\n+\n+    Returns:\n+        A list of dicts, one per input row, keyed by PUBLIC_COLUMNS.\n+    \"\"\"\n     out = []\n     for row in rows:\n         out.append({c: row[c] for c in PUBLIC_COLUMNS})\n"}]
